    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106326" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδερ-ος</span></b> , ὁ<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ʽὕδωῤ</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδρωψ</span>
			, <i>dropsy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Int.</u>
				22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1150b33
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδέρῳ νοσήματι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					486
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕ. εἰς ἀμίδα</span>”
				<i>diabetes,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					8.394
				</span></i>
			; cf. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδεροῦν</span></b>  ( 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ὕδερον</span>
			), which is cited from <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i> by <i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i> (but 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὑδρηλὸν χωρίον</span>
			 acc. to Epicles ap. eund.), prob. with ref. to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδρωπες</span> in <i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>.</div>
